cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dal, please cite it as below, and cite the datasets you use (see NOTICE.md)."
title: "dal: a lightweight single-object tracker and long-term holding benchmark for search-and-rescue drones"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The dal authors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sashapiscivca-svg/dal"
keywords:
  - search and rescue
  - visual object tracking
  - correlation filter
  - Kalman filter
  - drones
  - tiny objects
  - long-term tracking benchmark
  - Raspberry Pi
abstract: >-
  dal keeps a box on a person in drone video after an operator or a detector has pointed at them. The recommended tracker is
  training-free (MOSSE correlation filter, Kalman filter, camera-motion compensation) and runs on a Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W.
  The release includes a long-term holding benchmark (Survival@N) on openly licensed civilian datasets and a small learned
  tracker with a spiking motion module for research.
